00:09:04.240 --> 00:09:05.778
- Hi Hannah, I'm Grace.

00:09:05.778 --> 00:09:07.000
- And I'm D'Vante.

00:09:07.000 --> 00:09:08.050
- And we want to share a recipe

00:09:08.050 --> 00:09:09.821
for Bahamian guava duff with you.

00:09:09.821 --> 00:09:12.740
- What you'll find is
that this dessert recipe

00:09:12.740 --> 00:09:13.677
is something that's used

00:09:13.677 --> 00:09:16.020
in many different Bahamian households.

00:09:16.020 --> 00:09:16.853
Enjoy!

00:09:16.853 --> 00:09:18.840
- Here are my guava preserves.

00:09:18.840 --> 00:09:20.710
A dollar? A deal!

00:09:20.710 --> 00:09:25.710
A guava duff is a sweet,
fruit-filled cake-ish roll

00:09:26.600 --> 00:09:28.550
that's boiled instead of baked.

00:09:28.550 --> 00:09:31.090
So I cut in a bunch of shortening,

00:09:31.090 --> 00:09:33.560
and then I added some
baking powder and salt.

00:09:33.560 --> 00:09:35.030
So I'm nervous about this;

00:09:35.030 --> 00:09:37.753
I don't know how thin I'm
supposed to roll this dough out.

00:09:37.753 --> 00:09:40.640
I also had to roll it out
with a bottle of wine,

00:09:40.640 --> 00:09:42.610
because I don't have a rolling pin.

00:09:42.610 --> 00:09:44.550
I'm going to do a good amount.

00:09:44.550 --> 00:09:46.810
Oh geez, okay. Did I do this right?

00:09:46.810 --> 00:09:48.670
When I went to roll it up,

00:09:48.670 --> 00:09:52.260
I think I had rolled the
dough a little too thick,

00:09:52.260 --> 00:09:54.527
so all of my guava was spilling out

00:09:54.527 --> 00:09:58.370
and just getting smushed by
the heaviness of this loaf.

00:09:58.370 --> 00:10:02.407
Now I'm supposed to seal the ends.

00:10:02.407 --> 00:10:05.060
Oh gosh, I have just a handful of jam.

00:10:05.060 --> 00:10:08.080
Got this all wrapped up in its blanket.

00:10:08.080 --> 00:10:11.200
So the boiling aspect
of this duff, I think,

00:10:11.200 --> 00:10:12.830
keeps it really, really --

00:10:12.830 --> 00:10:14.300
I don't want to say this word --

00:10:14.300 --> 00:10:16.220
M-O-I-S-T,

00:10:16.220 --> 00:10:19.770
and makes it more of a pudding-y cake

00:10:19.770 --> 00:10:21.590
instead of a dry cake.

00:10:21.590 --> 00:10:23.240
It was really the moment of truth,

00:10:23.240 --> 00:10:24.100
when I unrolled it,

00:10:24.100 --> 00:10:27.300
to see if all of my guava had spilled out,

00:10:27.300 --> 00:10:30.920
so when I unrolled it,
it looked pretty good.

00:10:30.920 --> 00:10:32.300
I was shocked.

00:10:32.300 --> 00:10:34.815
I really hope I get that
spiral in the middle.

00:10:34.815 --> 00:10:35.648
(gasps)

00:10:35.648 --> 00:10:38.210
Ooh. Oh no, it's leaking!
Why did I do this?

00:10:38.210 --> 00:10:39.620
Oh (beep). Okay.

00:10:39.620 --> 00:10:41.260
The spiral needed a little work.

00:10:41.260 --> 00:10:43.705
I have some rum cream sauce on here.

00:10:43.705 --> 00:10:45.380
(Wyatt gasps)
- [Jackson] What is that?

00:10:45.380 --> 00:10:47.230
- [Hannah] Ooh it's dessert!

00:10:47.230 --> 00:10:50.151
I gave it to the boys, and
their minds were blown.

00:10:50.151 --> 00:10:52.645
- [Both] Mmm.
(Hannah laughs)

00:10:52.645 --> 00:10:54.810
- [Jackson] Tastes like apple pie.

00:10:54.810 --> 00:10:55.650
- [Hannah] Do you like it?

00:10:55.650 --> 00:10:56.490
- [Jackson] Mm-hmm.

00:10:56.490 --> 00:10:57.430
- [Wyatt] Uh-huh.
- [Jackson] Love it.

00:10:57.430 --> 00:11:00.470
- [Hannah] It's like a fluffier
apple pie, though, right?

00:11:00.470 --> 00:11:01.303
10 out of 10?

00:11:03.613 --> 00:11:04.446
(gasps)

00:11:04.446 --> 00:11:06.110
Wow!

00:11:06.110 --> 00:11:09.260
It's like if pie crust and
cinnamon rolls had a baby.

00:11:09.260 --> 00:11:11.640
I've never had a pastry like this.

00:11:11.640 --> 00:11:13.110
This is delicious.

00:11:13.110 --> 00:11:18.110
(singing) Going to Peru
tonight for dinner.

00:11:18.570 --> 00:11:20.950
We made green arroz con pollo.

00:11:20.950 --> 00:11:23.170
It is a chicken and rice dish

00:11:23.170 --> 00:11:24.961
that's all cooked in one pot

00:11:24.961 --> 00:11:27.741
with this amazing green sauce.

00:11:27.741 --> 00:11:29.800
(sniffs) Mmm, that smells so good.

00:11:29.800 --> 00:11:31.820
I started out by browning the chicken.

00:11:31.820 --> 00:11:34.190
That chicken looks nice.

00:11:34.190 --> 00:11:37.530
In the chicken drippings,
I'm going to toast the rice.

00:11:37.530 --> 00:11:39.923
I added the green sauce
and stock to my rice

00:11:39.923 --> 00:11:41.530
(pan sizzles) Oh (beep)

00:11:41.530 --> 00:11:43.733
Oh my god, okay, that heat's too hot.

00:11:43.733 --> 00:11:45.570
Okay, that was very intense.

00:11:45.570 --> 00:11:47.710
I laid the chicken on top and
then you just let it cook.

00:11:47.710 --> 00:11:49.570
When I finally pulled it out,

00:11:49.570 --> 00:11:50.816
it was beautifully green,

00:11:50.816 --> 00:11:53.960
the chicken looked super juicy,

00:11:53.960 --> 00:11:56.640
and the rice looked really
fluffy and delicious.

00:11:56.640 --> 00:11:58.730
Everybody loved this dish.

00:11:58.730 --> 00:12:00.300
Even Henry loved this dish.

00:12:00.300 --> 00:12:02.440
Henry actually got to eat this for dinner.

00:12:02.440 --> 00:12:04.082
You like it?

00:12:04.082 --> 00:12:04.915
(Henry vocalizes)

00:12:04.915 --> 00:12:05.748
- [Hannah] Yeah.

00:12:05.748 --> 00:12:07.868
- [Matt] This is probably
my favorite, I think.

00:12:07.868 --> 00:12:08.701
- [Hannah] Really?

00:12:08.701 --> 00:12:09.534
- [Matt] Yeah.

00:12:09.534 --> 00:12:10.367
- [Hannah] It's always a good day

00:12:10.367 --> 00:12:12.030
when everyone enjoys the food.

00:12:12.030 --> 00:12:13.720
This dish was really easy;

00:12:13.720 --> 00:12:17.190
I could see it becoming a
staple recipe in our house.

00:12:17.190 --> 00:12:18.590
Wow.

00:12:18.590 --> 00:12:20.227
It's so flavorful.

00:12:20.227 --> 00:12:21.120
- [Hannah] Thumbs up?

00:12:21.120 --> 00:12:23.309
- [Matt] Oh, yeah.

00:12:23.309 --> 00:12:26.040
- We're making mofongo tonight.

00:12:26.040 --> 00:12:27.840
Mofongo is a dish made of plantains

00:12:27.840 --> 00:12:31.110
and crispy pork skins which
are also called chicharrones.

00:12:31.110 --> 00:12:33.640
It's typically served with a stew

00:12:33.640 --> 00:12:36.360
or it can be stuffed with
meat or stuffed with food,

00:12:36.360 --> 00:12:39.260
but it's all compacted
into a little mound.

00:12:39.260 --> 00:12:40.930
I'm back with the plantains.

00:12:40.930 --> 00:12:44.820
I did fry them and I really
feel like that's my calling now.

00:12:44.820 --> 00:12:47.300
Jackson now thinks he's a vlogger,

00:12:47.300 --> 00:12:49.770
so he kind of took over
the filming for this one.

00:12:49.770 --> 00:12:53.366
- She's all the way
over there in her room,

00:12:53.366 --> 00:12:56.784
so that means I can secretly dance.

00:12:56.784 --> 00:12:58.877
- Watch out, I have a sharp knife.

00:12:58.877 --> 00:12:59.710
(Jackson gasps)

00:12:59.710 --> 00:13:03.510
So I'm going to mash the
plantains with these pork skins,

00:13:03.510 --> 00:13:06.320
crispy pork skins, and some garlic.

00:13:06.320 --> 00:13:07.610
I packed it all in a bowl,

00:13:07.610 --> 00:13:09.460
and then went to flip it to take it out,

00:13:09.460 --> 00:13:12.400
and that's where I met a roadblock.

00:13:12.400 --> 00:13:13.320
Oh, no.

00:13:13.320 --> 00:13:16.225
(gasps) I'm stuck.

00:13:16.225 --> 00:13:17.510
Oh, there we go.

00:13:17.510 --> 00:13:19.890
It looked incredible, it smelled amazing,

00:13:19.890 --> 00:13:21.670
I plated it with a beef stew

00:13:21.670 --> 00:13:22.750
because it looked hearty

00:13:22.750 --> 00:13:24.770
and it looked like it
would go along with it,

00:13:24.770 --> 00:13:27.313
and I could not wait to
see the boys' reactions.

00:13:28.529 --> 00:13:31.840
- [Jackson] Mmm, mmm, mmm. So good.

00:13:31.840 --> 00:13:32.790
- They loved it.

00:13:32.790 --> 00:13:35.790
I think Jackson probably
loved it most of all.

00:13:35.790 --> 00:13:37.870
He was slurping it up.

00:13:37.870 --> 00:13:40.950
Wyatt wouldn't use a fork or anything

00:13:40.950 --> 00:13:43.930
to get the mofongo off the dome.

00:13:43.930 --> 00:13:47.010
Wyatt is just -- he is who he is,

00:13:47.010 --> 00:13:49.520
and we love him for it, and that's it.

00:13:49.520 --> 00:13:52.010
Oh my gosh, I can demolish this
whole thing in two seconds.

00:13:52.010 --> 00:13:53.440
This is delicious.

00:13:53.440 --> 00:13:54.635
- Oh my god.
- [Hannah] 10 out of 10?

00:13:54.635 --> 00:13:55.660
- 10 out of 10.

00:13:55.660 --> 00:13:57.058
- [Hannah] What do you think, honey?

00:13:57.058 --> 00:13:57.980
(Henry vocalizes)

00:13:57.980 --> 00:13:59.140
You want more?

00:13:59.140 --> 00:14:00.870
I will definitely be making this again.

00:14:00.870 --> 00:14:02.750
It's really easy to find ingredients,

00:14:02.750 --> 00:14:03.666
it's easy to make,

00:14:03.666 --> 00:14:05.680
and the kids really enjoyed it.

00:14:05.680 --> 00:14:07.610
- [Jackson] Puerto Rico
knows what they're doing.

00:14:07.610 --> 00:14:09.400
- I feel like we hit the jackpot.

00:14:09.400 --> 00:14:12.260
These dishes now go in
my Rolodex of recipes

00:14:12.260 --> 00:14:14.030
that I want to make forever.

00:14:14.030 --> 00:14:15.510
And I want to keep doing this,

00:14:15.510 --> 00:14:18.130
because I think it's a really
important learning experience

00:14:18.130 --> 00:14:19.370
for teaching them

00:14:19.370 --> 00:14:21.360
about appreciating other cultures

00:14:21.360 --> 00:14:24.700
and appreciating other foods
and smells and textures

00:14:24.700 --> 00:14:25.840
and ways of eating.

00:14:25.840 --> 00:14:27.670
So I want to also thank all of you

00:14:27.670 --> 00:14:29.120
for sending me your recipes.

00:14:29.120 --> 00:14:30.680
I wish I could document them all,

00:14:30.680 --> 00:14:32.790
but I am certainly making them all.

00:14:32.790 --> 00:14:36.220
My kids and I are so
appreciative and grateful

00:14:36.220 --> 00:14:38.480
to have these special dishes in our house.

00:14:38.480 --> 00:14:39.540
So that's all for now.

00:14:39.540 --> 00:14:42.460
I'm Hannah, and tell
me what country's food

00:14:42.460 --> 00:14:43.360
we should try next.

00:14:43.360 --> 00:14:45.200
Please link me some recipes

00:14:45.200 --> 00:14:46.033
and please let me know

00:14:46.033 --> 00:14:48.150
if you'd like to see a Part 3 of this.

00:14:48.150 --> 00:14:50.130
Now if you'll please excuse me,

00:14:50.130 --> 00:14:52.020
Henry and I have some cuddles to do.

00:14:52.020 --> 00:14:53.316
Did you like the food?

00:14:53.316 --> 00:14:55.081
'Til next time.

00:14:55.081 --> 00:14:58.248
(bouncy plucky music)

